1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,137
A landing page presents one offer on one page.

2
00:00:04,137 --> 00:00:08,541
In this video, you build one from blocks with the Flows module, and

3
00:00:08,541 --> 00:00:12,040
then use a layer to show a widget only on that page.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:15,660
Along the way, you meet widgets, zones and conditions.

5
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:24,136
The Flows module adds a Flow to a content type, such as a page.

6
00:00:24,136 --> 00:00:27,956
A Flow holds the blocks of that one page, and you arrange them

7
00:00:27,956 --> 00:00:29,360
in the page editor.

8
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:31,831
Each block is a widget:

9
00:00:31,831 --> 00:00:35,749
a content item whose content type has the Widget stereotype.

10
00:00:35,749 --> 00:00:40,081
Widgets can also go into zones, the named places of a theme layout,

11
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:42,040
such as Content and Footer.

12
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:46,024
The Layers module decides where those widgets show.

13
00:00:46,024 --> 00:00:49,541
A layer has a name and a rule, and its widgets appear on

14
00:00:49,541 --> 00:00:51,810
every page where the rule is true.

15
00:00:56,110 --> 00:00:59,423
In the admin menu, open Content, Content Items.

16
00:00:59,423 --> 00:01:01,174
Select New, then Page.

17
00:01:01,174 --> 00:01:07,800
Enter the title Spring Workshop and the permalink spring-workshop, which is the address of the page.

18
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:12,359
Below the permalink, the Flow holds the blocks of the page.

19
00:01:12,359 --> 00:01:17,328
Select the plus button, Add Widget, to list the widget types of the site:

20
00:01:17,328 --> 00:01:21,040
Blockquote, Container, Image, Paragraph and Raw Html.

21
00:01:21,504 --> 00:01:25,753
Choose Paragraph, and type the opening text of the page in Content.

22
00:01:25,753 --> 00:01:29,014
The card has its own size menu and alignment menu.

23
00:01:29,475 --> 00:01:31,965
The size menu shows 100%.

24
00:01:31,965 --> 00:01:36,865
Choose 50%, and the card narrows to half of the editor.

25
00:01:37,359 --> 00:01:42,231
Add a second block, a Blockquote, and type a customer quote in Quote.

26
00:01:42,231 --> 00:01:47,559
Set its size to 50% as well, then open the alignment menu and choose Center.

27
00:01:54,019 --> 00:01:58,028
Drag the Blockquote card by its handle to the left of the Paragraph card.

28
00:01:58,028 --> 00:02:01,479
The order of the cards is the order of the blocks on the page.

29
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:03,205
Select Publish.

30
00:02:03,205 --> 00:02:07,090
A notification confirms that your Page has been published.

31
00:02:07,541 --> 00:02:09,383
Open the address of the page.

32
00:02:09,383 --> 00:02:12,854
The title is in the page header, and the two blocks sit side

33
00:02:12,854 --> 00:02:15,221
by side below it, with the quote first.

34
00:02:19,521 --> 00:02:21,010
Open Design, Widgets.

35
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:24,815
The Widgets and Layers page lists the zones on the left and the

36
00:02:24,815 --> 00:02:26,248
layers on the right.

37
00:02:26,248 --> 00:02:31,541
This site was set up with the Blog recipe, which provides two layers, Always and Homepage.

38
00:02:31,992 --> 00:02:33,827
Select Edit on Always.

39
00:02:33,827 --> 00:02:39,527
Its rule is one Boolean condition set to true, so its widgets show on every page.

40
00:02:39,527 --> 00:02:43,392
The Homepage layer uses a Homepage condition instead.

41
00:02:43,843 --> 00:02:47,803
Back on the Widgets and Layers page, select Add under Layers.

42
00:02:47,803 --> 00:02:52,293
Enter the name Workshop, write a short description, and select Create.

43
00:02:52,746 --> 00:02:56,963
The layer is saved, and its page asks for at least one condition.

44
00:02:56,963 --> 00:03:00,468
Without a condition, a layer never shows its widgets.

45
00:03:00,468 --> 00:03:03,616
Select Add to open the list of available rules.

46
00:03:04,079 --> 00:03:08,760
The Available Rules dialog lists a card for each condition, such as Boolean

47
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:15,291
condition, Content type condition, Culture condition, Homepage condition, Role condition and Url condition.

48
00:03:15,291 --> 00:03:18,239
The Filter box narrows the cards as you type.

49
00:03:18,815 --> 00:03:22,885
Type Url in the Filter box, and choose the Url condition.

50
00:03:22,885 --> 00:03:28,375
Keep the operation Equals, enter the value /spring-workshop, and select Create.

51
00:03:28,375 --> 00:03:30,765
The condition is saved at once.

52
00:03:31,293 --> 00:03:33,309
The rule lists its condition.

53
00:03:33,309 --> 00:03:37,167
When a rule has several conditions, all of them must be true.

54
00:03:37,167 --> 00:03:40,103
A separate video covers the other conditions.

55
00:03:44,403 --> 00:03:46,071
Open Settings, Zones.

56
00:03:46,071 --> 00:03:51,135
Available zones for Layers holds a comma separated list, and the Blog recipe

57
00:03:51,135 --> 00:03:53,543
fills it with Content and Footer.

58
00:03:53,998 --> 00:03:57,657
The hint under the field reminds you that the theme layout has to

59
00:03:57,657 --> 00:04:01,058
render each zone, because zones do not render automatically.

60
00:04:05,358 --> 00:04:09,023
Back on Design, Widgets, each zone has an Add Widget button.

61
00:04:09,023 --> 00:04:13,132
The Footer zone already holds the footer widget of the Always layer.

62
00:04:13,132 --> 00:04:16,298
Open Add Widget in that zone, and choose Paragraph.

63
00:04:17,336 --> 00:04:22,473
Enter a title, and check Render title so that the title appears with the widget.

64
00:04:22,473 --> 00:04:24,921
In The layer list, select Workshop.

65
00:04:24,921 --> 00:04:28,206
The layer controls the visibility of this widget.

66
00:04:31,905 --> 00:04:35,311
Type a short message in Content, and select Publish.

67
00:04:35,311 --> 00:04:38,248
Only a published widget appears on the site.

68
00:04:38,248 --> 00:04:40,185
A draft stays in the admin.

69
00:04:40,652 --> 00:04:44,414
The widget is listed in the Footer zone, tagged with its layer.

70
00:04:44,414 --> 00:04:49,102
Check Workshop in the layer list, and the widgets of that layer are highlighted.

71
00:04:49,671 --> 00:04:53,939
Drag the widget above the Footer widget to change the order in the zone.

72
00:04:53,939 --> 00:04:57,331
The position is saved at once, and an Undo link appears.

73
00:05:01,631 --> 00:05:03,162
Open the landing page.

74
00:05:03,162 --> 00:05:07,538
The footer shows the widget of the Workshop layer, with its title, because

75
00:05:07,538 --> 00:05:09,671
the rule is true at this address.

76
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,418
Open the homepage.

77
00:05:11,418 --> 00:05:15,141
The rule is false there, so the widget does not appear, while the

78
00:05:15,141 --> 00:05:17,500
footer widget of the Always layer does.

79
00:05:17,955 --> 00:05:22,919
Every widget of the Workshop layer follows this rule, in whichever zone it sits.

80
00:05:22,919 --> 00:05:27,075
To show a widget on other pages, create a layer with its own rule.

81
00:05:31,275 --> 00:05:34,231
Use a Flow for content that belongs to one page.

82
00:05:34,231 --> 00:05:37,954
Its blocks are stored in the page and edited with it, like the

83
00:05:37,954 --> 00:05:40,035
two blocks of the workshop page.

84
00:05:40,785 --> 00:05:43,835
Use a layer for content that appears on many pages.

85
00:05:43,835 --> 00:05:48,383
Its widgets are separate content items, edited from the Widgets page, and shown

86
00:05:48,383 --> 00:05:50,095
wherever the rule is true.

87
00:05:52,095 --> 00:05:53,561
That's a landing page:

88
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:56,966
a Flow arranges the blocks of one page, and a layer shows a

89
00:05:56,966 --> 00:05:59,113
widget only where its rule is true.

90
00:05:59,113 --> 00:06:00,475
Thanks for watching.

